      "mechanism": "packet absolute spans versus relative proportions",
      "before": "A30px short field could pass the4%-ratio predicate and fail the absolute bit-unit predicate under the same criterion, throwing at merge.",
      "after": "Relative ratios are a supplementary finite-profile criterion. Absolute span/offset/row proof stays required; complete wrapped-segment proof can replace only its unavailable relative projection."
    },
    {
      "mechanism": "actual overpaint versus source-fact credit",
      "before": "A fully opaque intrinsic image over a saved packet left source-fact:fields passed. This was an individual-fact false positive; the generic whole-drawing check was already unknown.",
      "after": "Later overlapping image/use extents withhold domain/chart/quantity carrier credit. Hidden and outside images retain positives; no image transparency or pixel decoder is invented."
    },
    {
      "mechanism": "explicit requirement layout",
      "before": "Pinned source explicitly requestsLR, but direction had been treated as advisory.",
      "after": "Source policy independently restored the required fact. Owned row/column box ranks with exposed captions qualify a connected simple chain; wrong-axis controls fail and ambiguous layouts stay unknown."
    }
